      "title": "OpenAI pledges to pay data-center power costs and disclose impacts",
      "content_html": "OpenAI on Nov. 5 announced a community compact for future U.S. AI campuses it owns and operates, pledging to cover electricity and grid-infrastructure costs, publish environmental and construction information, and work with unions on local hiring. It also said it would avoid nondisclosure agreements with public officials except for narrow security and commercial protections, and provide financial assurances if a project is delayed, reduced or canceled.\n\nA separate policy blueprint urges federal, state and local governments to require large power users to pay for the grid costs they add, disclose water, energy, noise and hiring data, and tie tax incentives to measurable commitments. The announcement followed the Nov. 3 election results and local votes against data-center projects. OpenAI’s chief global affairs officer, Chris Lehane, said the proposals had been in development since August, before the election. The compact applies to campuses OpenAI owns and operates, while the company’s proposed rules target the wider industry.",
